<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cölln</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cölln was a medieval town on an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spree">Spree</a>, the twin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> on the opposite bank. Its first record, in 1237, is taken as the founding date of Berlin. The two towns shared a common council from 1307 and were formally merged with neighbouring towns into the single city of Berlin in 1710.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/colln.jpg" alt="Cölln" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stern · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stadtviertel_in_Berlin-Mitte.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
